 ## Overview
-VolSDF Volume Rendering is a technique that performs volume integration using Signed Distance Functions (SDFs) as the underlying geometric representation instead of raw density fields [S2, unofficial]. It solves the optimization instability of learning raw densities by converting SDF values into volumetric densities using learnable scaling and shrinking coefficients (alpha and beta) before applying standard alpha compositing [S4]. Unlike [Volume SDF Rendering](1344-volume-sdf-rendering.md) which may use different weighting schemes, VolSDF explicitly learns these coefficients to ensure the volume rendering is alpha-invariant, meaning the magnitude of the density is globally tied to its sharpness [S4].
